.TH CHTTP_REQUEST_NEW_MP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_request_new_mp \- allocate and initialise an HTTP request with a custom allocator
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

chttp_request_t *chttp_request_new_mp(chttp_method_t method,
                                      const char *url,
                                      const chttp_request_body_t *body,
                                      ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mprocs,
                                      char **err_str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates a new chttp_request_t and copies the URL and, if non-NULL,
the body data and content_type string into privately owned buffers.
The caller may free its originals immediately after this call returns.

Pass NULL for body or use the CHTTP_NO_BODY macro when no request body
is needed (e.g. GET, DELETE).
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
method    HTTP method (CHTTP_GET, CHTTP_POST, ...).
url       Target URL; must not be NULL (copied into the request).
body      Pointer to a chttp_request_body_t, or NULL for no body.
mprocs    Custom allocator, or NULL for malloc/free.
err_str   Optional; receives a static error string on failure.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Pointer to the new request, or NULL on failure.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
All allocations use mprocs when non-NULL.
The request must remain alive until any chttpclient_do call using it
returns: the request's method/body/headers are read directly during
that synchronous call.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_request_new (3),
.BR chttp_request_set_header (3),
.BR chttp_request_free (3),
.BR chttpclient_do (3)
